usable_hours).","meta":{"dataset_build_id":"sg-8db7fb77e1eb","schema_version":"1.0.0","built_at_utc":"2026-11-14T16:54:19Z","time_scale":"UTC","conventions":{"time":"UTC, ISO 8601","azimuth":"degrees, 0 = north, 90 = east, clockwise, in [0, 360)","elevation":"degrees above the local horizontal","longitude":"degrees east, 0 to 360","visible_rule":"elevation_deg > skyline elevation at the body's azimuth (body centre point; apparent disc size not included)","lunar_day_hours":708.72,"reference_sphere_radius_m":1737400},"horizon_model":"lola_mask","mask_interpolation":"linear_between_bins","sources":[{"source_id":"jpl_horizons","name":"NASA/JPL Horizons observer tables","version":null,"url":"https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/api/horizons.api"},{"source_id":"lola_ldem_80s_80m","name":"NASA LOLA gridded elevation model LDEM_80S_80M","version":"v2.0","url":"https://imbrium.mit.edu/DATA/LOLA_GDR/POLAR/IMG/LDEM_80S_80M.IMG"},{"source_id":"stargazer_cost_model","name":"Stargazer Monte Carlo cost model (backend/cost_mc.py)","version":null,"url":null},{"source_id":"clps_public_awards","name":"CLPS task order award values (as noted in cost_mc.py)","version":null,"url":null}],"quality_flags":[{"code":"COST_ANCHORS_UNVERIFIED","severity":"warning","scope":"dataset","message":"Delivery-price anchors with no recorded source: Peregrine, CP-22, IM-5. Fill source_url, verified_by and verified_on in backend/data/cost_sources.csv and rebuild.","fix_order":"F7"},{"code":"COORDINATES_UNVERIFIED","severity":"info","scope":"site:malapert","message":"Site coordinates and notes come from repo comments with no cited source. Add the citation to backend/data/site_notes.json to mark them verified.","fix_order":"F5"},{"code":"HORIZONS_ALTITUDE_NOT_SITE_HEIGHT","severity":"info","scope":"site:malapert","message":"The Horizons ephemeris was fetched for an observer at 0.00 km above the reference sphere; the LOLA ground height is 5.13 km. Terrain is handled by the horizon mask, not by the ephemeris. Upper bound on the direction error from the height difference (height / distance): about 0.00082 deg for Earth at its closest (356,400 km) and 0.0000020 deg for the Sun. Not yet checked against a re-fetch with the real altitude.","fix_order":"F4"},{"code":"COORDINATES_UNVERIFIED","severity":"info","scope":"site:shackleton","message":"Site coordinates and notes come from repo comments with no cited source. Add the citation to backend/data/site_notes.json to mark them verified.","fix_order":"F5"},{"code":"HORIZONS_ALTITUDE_NOT_SITE_HEIGHT","severity":"info","scope":"site:shackleton","message":"The Horizons ephemeris was fetched for an observer at 0.00 km above the reference sphere; the LOLA ground height is 1.72 km. Terrain is handled by the horizon mask, not by the ephemeris. Upper bound on the direction error from the height difference (height / distance): about 0.00028 deg for Earth at its closest (356,400 km) and 0.0000007 deg for the Sun. Not yet checked against a re-fetch with the real altitude.","fix_order":"F4"},{"code":"COORDINATES_UNVERIFIED","severity":"info","scope":"site:mons-mouton","message":"Site coordinates and notes come from repo comments with no cited source. Add the citation to backend/data/site_notes.json to mark them verified.","fix_order":"F5"},{"code":"HORIZONS_ALTITUDE_NOT_SITE_HEIGHT","severity":"info","scope":"site:mons-mouton","message":"The Horizons ephemeris was fetched for an observer at 0.00 km above the reference sphere; the LOLA ground height is 5.32 km. Terrain is handled by the horizon mask, not by the ephemeris. Upper bound on the direction error from the height difference (height / distance): about 0.00086 deg for Earth at its closest (356,400 km) and 0.0000021 deg for the Sun. Not yet checked against a re-fetch with the real altitude.","fix_order":"F4"},{"code":"BEST_OVERLAP_IN_EPHEMERIS_FILES_IS_FLAT","severity":"info","scope":"dataset","message":"The best_overlap value inside ephemeris_long/*.json assumes a flat horizon (elevation > 0). It is not loaded. This database recomputes best overlap per lunar day for each horizon model; the website's getBestOverlap still reads the flat value until it is switched to the API.","fix_order":"F2"},{"code":"MASK_LOOKUP_RULES_DIFFER_IN_REPO","severity":"info","scope":"dataset","message":"The website reads the skyline by linear interpolation between whole-degree bins; the committed cost_mc.py uses floor(azimuth). This database uses linear interpolation for all visibility and for the default terrain-aware cost run, and also stores a floor(azimuth) cost run so earlier numbers reproduce.","fix_order":"F3"},{"code":"UNCERTAINTY_IS_SKYLINE_ONLY","severity":"info","scope":"dataset","message":"Optimistic and pessimistic windows shift the whole skyline by -/+ sigma (0.3 degrees unless changed, a team assumption). They do not include ephemeris error, the apparent size of the Sun or Earth, or site position error.","fix_order":null},{"code":"POINT_SOURCE_BODIES","severity":"info","scope":"dataset","message":"The Sun and Earth are treated as points at their centres. The Sun's disc is about 0.5 degrees wide and the Earth's about 1.9 degrees as seen from the Moon, so real rises and sets are gradual.","fix_order":null},{"code":"SITE_LIST_DIFFERS_FROM_PLAN_DOC","severity":"warning","scope":"dataset","message":"STARGAZER_Project_Overview_Plan.md names 'Wiechert Circle' (and 'Shackleton Crater') as sites; the data has malapert, mons-mouton, shackleton. The database follows the data. See backend/docs/ADD_A_SITE.md to add a site; the team should correct the plan doc and slides.","fix_order":"F5"}],"caveat":"Geometric visibility only: whether the centre of the Sun or Earth is above the terrain skyline. Sun visibility is not electrical power and Earth visibility is not a working radio link; no power-system or link-budget model is included."}}